Run the test suites on Windows.

Five API tests use alarm and SIGALRM (terminate, cipasir, parcompwrite),
fork (cfreeze) or setenv (apitrace). MinGW provides none of them, so the
tests fail to compile. Skip them when the compiler targets Windows.

example_tracer writes its proofs under /tmp. A native Windows program
resolves that against the root of the current drive, which usually has
no tmp directory, so on Windows it writes them to the working directory.

The CNF suite checks each solution with precochk, which compares the
solver's output byte by byte against '\n'. On Windows the solver writes
its output in text mode, as '\r\n', and precochk rejects every
satisfiable result. Skip the '\r' as it reads.

Upstream: not submitted
Applies-to: all environments

--- a/test/api/run.sh
+++ b/test/api/run.sh
@@ -67,7 +67,24 @@
   status=$?
 }
 
+# These tests use 'alarm', 'fork' or 'setenv', which Windows does not have.
+
+posixonly=" terminate cfreeze cipasir parcompwrite apitrace "
+case x"`$CXX -dumpmachine 2>/dev/null`" in
+  *mingw*|*windows*) windows=yes;;
+  *) windows=no;;
+esac
+
 run () {
+  case "$posixonly" in
+    *" $1 "*)
+      if test $windows = yes
+      then
+        msg "skipping API test ${HILITE}'$1'${NORMAL} on Windows"
+        return
+      fi
+      ;;
+  esac
   msg "running API test ${HILITE}'$1'${NORMAL}"
   if [ -f $tests/$1.c ]
   then
